      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"value\" is local so no other entity can change it, so having the lock around the conditional doesn\u0027t protect anything. This would be the same:\n```\n  if (value \u003c 0) {\n    spin_lock_irqsave(\u0026gi-\u003espinlock, flags);\n    value \u003d composite_setup(gadget, c);\n    spin_unlock_irqrestore(\u0026gi-\u003espinlock, flags);\n  }\n```\nDoes this mean that the bug is really in `composite_setup()`? Do we know that this scenario can only happen with Android?",
      "revId": "1a74960dfffe0bf7fc077adfa488aad0c0548c36",
